WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.090
Char and Kamille returned to space
to find...

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.690
...a larger than usual Titans force
attacking the Argama.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.760
The Argama proceeded to "Colony 13",
reserved as a neutral site within Side Two.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:49.030
They went there for replenishments
and repairs to the ship.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:54.110
By The Lake

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.110
This is the Titans' space fortress, Gryps.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:05.160
Gryps has now been divided in two.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.390
Now, A Baoa Qu, which was renamed
the Gate of Zedan...

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:11.890
...and Luna II serve jointly
as the Titans' bases.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.400
It's still too soon to use the Colony Laser.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.840
Your Excellency, you said yourself
that we cannot ignore Char's speech.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.070
I haven't forgotten.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.070
I'd like to suggest attacking Granada
at once ...

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:34.380
...but there's not enough time
to move Gryps 2 to the firing point.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.780
It's always possible
for the Earth Federation Government...

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.820
...to overturn recent decisions, after all!

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.010
I've taken steps to ensure
such ridiculous things...

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.030
...are never accepted
as legislation.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.690
You don't seem too confident.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.360
Are you suggesting treaties
are made to be broken?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.430
I can't leave some wicked man
like Scirocco in charge.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.100
I'll go myself.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.340
With the Dogosse Gier?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.340
Yes!

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.440
Please be assured, one push from me
and the A.E.U.G. will no longer exist.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.450
After that, we'll take care of
Haman Karn and Scirocco!

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.980
Naturally.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.020
- Has she gotten in?
- <i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.720
<i>She's gone directly to Colony 13.</i>

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.420
<i>I'll have her try a number of options.</i>

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.360
Okay.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.130
You're very thorough.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.260
Was that about Rosamia Badam?

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.300
Yes, sir.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.840
- She's a good girl.
- Yes, sir!

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:33.970
Bask is in a hurry to organize troops
with Cyber-Newtypes at the core?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.040
Yes.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.380
Ever since that broadcast from Dakar.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.420
There's not enough time for that.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.090
It's impossible to gather
the number needed.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.050
They're exploring the possibility...

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.650
...that the woman from the Argama
could be one as well.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.830
What could they be thinking?

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.330
Reccoa Londe is normal.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.960
She's just a woman with a strong
need to rely on others.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.500
But she pretends to be tough,
so she ends up betraying herself.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.170
Is she not a spy?

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.040
That's nothing but
a vulgar presumption.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.010
Just watch her.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.180
She'll become a very valuable pilot
for the Jupitris.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.110
I want you to protect the Gate of Zedan.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.250
Therefore...!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.980
Never mind me, sir.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.920
If Captain Bask wishes to use
the Dogosse Gier...

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.860
...I shall return it with pleasure.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.120
We will continue to supply
the Jupitris indefinitely.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.720
Do not forget to back up Bask.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:31.900
Yes, sir!

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.000
- You can count on me, sir.
- That's honorable of you.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.040
Captain!

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.070
There's one A.E.U.G. vessel from which
I feel especially strong pressure.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.040
The Argama?

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.210
Please be cautious.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.550
Scirocco.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:48.680
One thing I dislike about you...

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:53.250
...is that you believe no person exists
with abilities superior to yourself.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.760
Stop looking down on us!

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.750
- Do you need a ride?
- Please.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:23.790
Okay!

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.920
<i>Welcome to the land of mountains</i>
<i>and lakes, Morgarten!</i>

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.600
<i>The boarding spot for the linear cars</i>
<i>is to your right.</i>

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.230
Please take me to the hotel!

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.400
Most certainly.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.600
Here we go!

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:48.900
Boy, do they have to get that excited?!

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.070
It's to be expected.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:53.480
It's the first time they've come to a place
like this since leaving Earth.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:10.130
This colony has no military facilities...

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.530
...but the Argama is docked
in the spaceport.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.600
Could it mean there's an A.E.U.G.
supply factory...

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.970
...mixed in among
the civilian companies?

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.640
All right!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.410
Be quiet!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.740
This linear car doesn't belong to you,
you know!

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:31.820
No, it couldn't be.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.950
- Are you sure?
- About you taking time off?

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:37.320
Dr. Hasan told you
to get some rest, right?

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.250
I'm talking about your workload!

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.590
I can do it alone!

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.500
All I'm doing is confirming the goods
we're receiving.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:48.660
Meanwhile, be careful. Be sure
no one recognizes you're a soldier.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.370
Anxious looks like yours
are the most dangerous.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.670
We're going!

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.040
Wow!

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.450
Awesome! It's like we're flying!

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.830
Lucerne...!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.140
Wow! What are those, Kamille?!

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.370
They're agricultural plants.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.640
They grow vegetables and raise livestock.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.180
Why are there so many?

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.510
What a dumb question!

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.950
Otherwise they'd run out of food!

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.210
There's another reason.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.850
By having many facilities you can have
a variety of vegetables...

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.220
...from different seasons,
whenever you want them.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.380
I get it!

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.760
Those guys from the A.E.U.G.
haven't been here for half a day.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.920
What a drag.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.220
Maybe they know we're here.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.390
- I'm going!
- Wait for me!

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.760
Hey! Calm down, you two!

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.300
Brother?

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.870
Brother!

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.780
Wow!

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:43.950
- Cool! Mountains!
- Gee!

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.290
We're surrounded by mountains!
How beautiful!

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.450
I wonder if the Alps on Earth are like this?

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:51.260
It's like this in photos, isn't it?

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.060
- Hurry, over here!
- Come here!

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.500
Okay, here I go!

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.240
Kamille!

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:04.140
Brother, is that you?

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:07.700
What's this?!

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.640
It's a ride being pulled by a horse!

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.200
- Want to ride it?
- Can we ride it?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.910
Fa!

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:16.820
You're all too fast for me!

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:19.010
Anyone can ride this horse.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.210
Snap the reins!

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:23.590
Right.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.630
Then the horse will walk forward.
Now, pull the ropes!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.160
That's right!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.530
And that's all, it'll take you to Besschen.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.170
Brother!

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.300
I knew it was you, Brother!

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:45.100
Huh?! Wh-What is it?! Wait a minute!

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.080
Pay your fare when you get to Besschen!

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.180
Okay!

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.940
Kamille's little sister?!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.350
Boy, you're pretty!

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:52.350
Thank you.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.690
Sit down or you'll hurt yourselves!

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.050
Brother!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.460
I-I have no clue who you are!

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:01.130
You haven't changed one bit, Brother.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.360
You used to always tease me like this.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.160
Who are you, anyway?!

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:06.220
Rosammy Badam.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:10.200
What's the big idea
clinging onto Kamille's arm?!

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:11.870
Ouch!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.370
You must be my brother's girlfriend.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.340
I see.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:20.950
I'd always imagined that if my brother
were to have a girlfriend...

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.040
...your type would suit him the best!

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:27.660
You're perfect for my brother!

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.550
R-Really?

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:30.850
Thank you.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:31.950
Is that so!

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.000
Kamille's little sister!

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.860
She looks old enough to be his big sister.

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:38.900
Guess she looks old for her age.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.090
But she's gorgeous!

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:44.300
That's right. I look mature for my age,
but that has its advantages!

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:47.340
Like attracting handsome boys?!

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:49.310
Shinta!

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.920
I can't help but think about it.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.920
They said the Argama is docked
at Colony 13.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.260
Nine mobile suits have been
ambushed in this area.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.600
I'll look around and then
return to the Argama.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.370
It's here!

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.340
It's reconnoitering all alone?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.710
It could be a decoy!

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.270
Even if it were, we'd still prevail!

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.610
- Let's go!
- You're right!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.790
It's the golden mobile suit!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.300
I'm sure that one belongs to the Argama.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:44.860
What should we do?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.490
That'll mark our tenth one.
I think it's quite fitting!

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:50.000
- <i>Y- You're right. Want to do it?!</i>
- Of course!

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:19.530
Listen.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.540
This person's name is Kamille.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.570
He's not your brother!

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:24.810
How come?

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.170
He's my brother.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.480
- You skirt-chaser!
- What's wrong with that!?

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.880
Don't you find it strange?!

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:35.110
I do! And that's why I'm finding out
what kind of girl she is!

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.480
Watch out, Brother!

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.820
- Wow!
- Sheep!

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.590
Far out! There are a whole lot of 'em!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.890
I know!

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.490
Look!

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:49.930
This is...!

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:51.490
It's Kamille!

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:52.870
It is!

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.660
Looks just like me.

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:56.400
Yes, he looks a lot like Kamille!

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:57.770
But that doesn't...!

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:00.210
During the Colony Drop
in the previous war...

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.710
...I lost my younger brother,
but my older brother was never found!

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.010
And now I've found him!

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.070
You can't be sure!

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.740
But he's with the ideal girlfriend
that I imagined.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:11.380
Me, his ideal girlfriend?

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.180
You're a perfect couple!

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:16.620
Shinta, don't get too close to the sheep,
or you'll get kicked!

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:23.490
She doesn't seem to be an enemy.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.370
I wonder what it is.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.970
I must be imagining it.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:45.080
It feels as if Amuro's in that colony.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:50.090
I'd damage the colony
if I fired from this angle!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.320
<i>Calm down! Don't punch a hole</i>
<i>in the colony!</i>

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:53.160
I know!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.090
Wait! The golden one's
moving away from the colony!

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:01.440
Gotcha!

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:05.810
Is that it?!

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:08.880
It avoided the shot! Kara!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.240
- <i>I'm going!</i>
- Roger!

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.020
Two Hizacks?!

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:20.980
Don't fire, Kara!

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.050
We'll get that golden one!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.120
We're losing! Come on, Fa!

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.990
It's impossible!
I'm not used to these things!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.360
Wait, Brother!

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.670
Qum, come on! We can't let Fa beat us!

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:42.910
You're not doing your job!
You've got to look ahead!

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:43.950
Sorry.

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:49.170
- Whose is it, I wonder.
- A volleyball?

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.310
- Why don't you take it over?
- Okay!

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:57.320
Outrageous! They're starting
a guerrilla war in this neutral zone!

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.630
Where'd he go!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:04.670
What?!

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:08.830
What?!

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.170
Don't fire, Kara!

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:16.040
Bastard!

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:20.920
Damn it!

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.810
Oops, he's done it!

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.690
The air's leaking! This isn't good!

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.030
They escaped into the colony!

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:45.400
Do they plan to wreck the colony?!

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:57.180
Sorama! <i>Sorama!!</i>

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.740
I've got to defeat the other one
without causing it to explode!

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:20.340
Rosammy!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:25.250
This time I'm riding with you, Brother.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:26.950
What did you do that for?!

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:28.610
Enough already!

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:30.220
Qum got off, did she?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.980
Rosammy.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.020
- Never mind her!
- But...!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.250
It's okay!

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.890
Frankly speaking,
you're too relaxed with her!

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:44.560
You're probably right!

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.930
But I'm not as frivolous
as you may think!

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:50.270
You live by the lake,
but you've never been in a boat?

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.570
Is that strange?

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:54.200
I'm good at rowing boats, you know!

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:59.140
- See? No problem, right?!
- You're right!

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.840
Huh? You're a girl?!

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:02.910
I am.

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:04.420
You're acting snobbish!

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.610
So what? Is that wrong?

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.320
Sure it's wrong!

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:15.400
You're wet.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:21.330
You people!

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.830
What are you trying to do with that child?!

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:26.600
She said she wants to ride the boat,
so we're letting her!

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.800
Come back here!

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.310
Don't let her do whatever she wishes.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.280
But...!

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:32.840
- See? Cold, isn't it?
- Yeah!

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.310
<i>Miss Mineva's laughing.</i>

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:39.310
I want to go a little further out there.

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:41.990
You don't like that lady?

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:44.550
She's all right. She serves me well.

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:48.160
That's the sort of talk
that makes you sound snobbish.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:51.170
Is that all you can say?

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:54.200
<i>Is that woman an enemy?</i>

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.900
<i>She has the scent of the A.E.U.G..</i>

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.830
It's time for her medicine!

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.270
Bring her back!

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:03.380
She says she doesn't want to return to you!

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:05.440
Woman! I said no such thing!

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.320
You're being jealous.

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:11.820
No I'm not!

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.410
You don't have a clue, do you?

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.750
You don't understand!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.450
That's my line!

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.700
She looks like Mineva Zabi.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:28.430
Kamille?

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.490
That's Haman Karn!

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:30.200
What?!

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.610
A Hizack!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:35.030
Take Miss Mineva inside!

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.750
- It's a Hizack!
- Rosammy!

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.370
Row back to shore and run!

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:44.480
Why, that's the A.E.U.G. pilot, Kamille.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:45.990
Come with me!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.350
Damn A.E.U.G.!

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.980
They were trying to kidnap Miss Mineva!

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:56.500
We're unlucky to have that
golden one for our tenth!

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.870
It's trying to escape
to a residential area!

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.270
That's one of the Gwadan's mobile suits!

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:10.450
Damn this thing!

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:19.280
Don't you realize
that we're in a colony?!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.130
Where'd it go?

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:37.110
Hey, pilot!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:39.970
Get out of the mobile suit!
You mustn't damage the colony any...!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.880
This is crazy!
Doesn't the pilot understand?!

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.150
Here goes!

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.550
G-Go up!

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:07.460
Don't look back! If you get blown away,
you won't survive!

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:09.270
Brother!

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:10.860
That's Lieutenant Quattro, isn't it?!

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:12.870
How come he's fighting in here?!

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:15.400
He must've come knowing
Haman Karn was here!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.470
We're safe now!

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:24.250
The door won't lock properly,
so we'd better keep moving.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.810
- I'm scared!
- Fa!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:30.560
It's okay, there's nothing
to be frightened about!

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.870
I managed to save this place
from destruction.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.500
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.580
Police officers are here to see you!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.780
I'm not surprised.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:54.080
Captain Bright is furious.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:57.020
Naturally. I violated
international law, after all!

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.710
Will you only be fined?

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:02.190
Not even that. The Hizacks I came across
are the Titan units...

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:07.230
...that have been breaking laws in
Colony 13 over the past two or three days.

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:10.530
It was also the Titans
that brought in weapons.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.330
I don't think I'll be punished.

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:16.800
We were on that lake, rowing a boat.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.070
Oh?

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:20.840
And I saw Haman Karn.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:21.840
Haman?!

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:23.380
And Mineva, too.

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:26.720
So that's what it was.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.070
- I sensed her there.
- You sensed it, Lieutenant?

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.550
That's why I hesitated...

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:34.720
...and ended up playing into
the enemy's hands.

00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:36.080
Is that so.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:39.820
Lieutenant, I'm glad you're okay!

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:43.130
- Are they here?
- Yes.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:47.530
Are you Lieutenant Quattro,
the pilot of the Hyaku Shiki?

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:48.040
Yes.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.840
Come with us to the police headquarters.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.970
We've received permission
from your captain.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.510
Yes, I'm aware.

00:21:58.550 --> 00:21:59.610
Who's that young lady?

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.650
She claims to be Kamille's younger sister.

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:03.080
It's a long story.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.490
Want some, Brother?

00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:12.750
Shall we go?

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:16.960
Does something bother you about her,
Lieutenant?

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:18.860
Yes.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:21.590
I-I'll have some!

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:23.700
Come on!

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:26.610
The ideal girlfriend
doesn't allow things like this!

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:30.810
But it's okay for me to do it!

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:31.810
Here!

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:32.850
Sure!

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.540 --> 00:23:50.000
The Argama encounters Reccoa
as it scouts Gryps 2.

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:55.070
Kamille can not understand
the "adults' logic" Reccoa refers to.

00:23:55.880 --> 00:23:58.980
While this is happening,
the Colony Laser of Gryps 2...

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:00.850
...destroys a colony.

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:07.530
Next on Mobile Suit Z eta Gundam,
"Activation of Gryps".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Activation of Gryps

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:10.260
You will see the tears of time.
